# Snippet: Mind Weave env when using HTTPS + your own domain (Path C)
# Copy values into backend/.env and frontend/.env — do not commit real secrets.
# Full backend template: backend/.env.example
# Walkthrough: docs/DEPLOYMENT_AND_NETWORK.md
#
# Replace example.com with your domain; api / app hostnames must match DNS and nginx (see docs/examples/nginx/).

# --- backend/.env (excerpt) ---
# Public HTTPS — Google OAuth redirect URIs use the API host on port 443 (no :8000 in the URL).
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://api.example.com/api/v1/auth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_WORKFLOW_REDIRECT_URI=https://api.example.com/api/v1/google-workflow/oauth/callback
# FRONTEND_URL=https://app.example.com
#
# Trust X-Forwarded-Proto from nginx on localhost (required for correct ASGI scope behind TLS).
# BEHIND_REVERSE_PROXY=true
#
# JSON lists in .env (see backend/.env.example):
# CORS_ORIGINS=["https://app.example.com","http://localhost:5173","http://127.0.0.1:5173"]
# TRUSTED_HOSTS=["localhost","127.0.0.1","testserver","api.example.com"]
#
# Production-like deployment (cookies Secure, strong SECRET_KEY, OpenAPI off when not local):
# APP_ENV=production
# SECRET_KEY=<openssl rand -hex 32 or similar, 32+ chars>
# SECURITY_ENABLE_HSTS=true
# OPEN_REGISTRATION=false

# --- frontend/.env (excerpt) ---
# Production build or dev when API is on another host:
# VITE_API_BASE=https://api.example.com
#
# Optional — Vite dev (`npm run dev`) behind HTTPS nginx (vite.config.ts reads these; not VITE_*):
# DEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS=app.example.com
# DEV_HMR_HOST=app.example.com
